      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1949 on land that once belonged to the Palestinian village Majdal Yaba, Rosh HaAyin began its modern era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosh_HaAyin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Declared a city in 1994, Rosh HaAyin spans roughly 16,000 dunams of the Sharon Plain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosh_HaAyin",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every roundabout in Rosh HaAyin features a statue of a musical instrument, turning traffic circles into mini concert halls.",
